{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He found him in a desert land.</b> He found the heart of His people — who is His portion — faithful before Him in the land of desert, as it says: לֶכְתֵּךְ אַחֲרַי בַּמִּדְבָּר (Jeremiah 2:2)." "<b>He encircled him.</b> Around Mount Sinai, as it says: וְהִגְבַּלְתָּ אֶת הָעָם סָבִיב (Exodus 19:12)." "<b>He instructed him.</b> As it says (Exodus 24:12): וְהַתּוֹרָה וְהַמִּצְוָה אֲשֶׁר כָּתַבְתִּי לְהוֹרֹתָם." "<b>He guarded him.</b> From the bondage of Egypt and from the angel of death, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Eiruvin 54a): ״חָרוּת עַל הַלּוּחוֹת — חֵרוּת מִמַּלְאַךְ הַמָּוֶת וּמִשִּׁעְבּוּד מַלְכֻיּוֹת״ — freedom from the angel of death and from the bondage of kingdoms." "<b>As the apple of His eye.</b> Just as He formed the pupil of a person's eye when He created it — He encircled the eye with layers of skin so that it would not be corrupted, it being naturally suited for that."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:01.201041186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}